---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro'
import AssertionCard from '../../components/AssertionCard.astro'
import ChartFigure from '../../components/ChartFigure.astro'
import { assertion } from '../../lib/feeds'
import { bar } from '../../lib/chart-spec'

const two = assertion('two-billion-in-the-countys-name')
const one = assertion('every-itemised-issue-was-one-hospital-system')
const what = assertion('what-a-conduit-issue-is')
const first = assertion('first-in-ohio-on-industrial-revenue-debt')
const check = assertion('two-instruments-within-three-per-cent')
const gasb = assertion('nine-hundred-million-in-the-year-the-rule-changed')
const gone = assertion('the-federal-file-stopped-carrying-it')

const all = assertion('forty-six-governments-raised-five-hundred-and-forty-six-million')
const halves = assertion('half-is-schools-and-a-thirtieth-is-townships')
const three = assertion('three-governments-are-nearly-half')
const ranks = assertion('thirty-sixth-on-revenue-and-twenty-first-on-spending')
const deficit = assertion('the-county-spends-more-than-it-raises')
const districts = assertion('a-special-district-is-whatever-ohio-made-a-government')

const owed = assertion('two-hundred-and-eighty-seven-million-owed')
const nine = assertion('nine-carry-ninety-six-per-cent-of-the-debt')
const least = assertion('the-county-owes-least-of-the-large-ones')
const fall = assertion('eighty-four-per-cent-that-did-not-happen')
const factor = assertion('a-factor-of-a-hundred-and-twelve')
const liab = assertion('long-term-debt-is-not-every-liability')

const noanswer = assertion('the-county-did-not-answer')
const schools = assertion('the-schools-answer-and-the-villages-do-not')
const rate = assertion('an-interest-rate-of-two-hundred-and-fifty-eight-per-cent')
const auditor = assertion('the-auditor-says-two-hundred-and-six-thousand')
const large = assertion('the-same-model-is-nearly-right-about-everything-large')
const flag = assertion('the-flag-travels-with-the-figure')

const ohioSpec = bar(
  first.figures.map((f) => f.label),
  first.figures.map((f) => f.value),
  { yTitle: 'Industrial revenue debt per resident', labelValues: true },
)
const gasbSpec = bar(
  gasb.figures.map((f) => f.label),
  gasb.figures.map((f) => f.value),
  { yTitle: 'Conduit debt outstanding', labelValues: true },
)
const fallSpec = bar(
  fall.figures.map((f) => f.label),
  fall.figures.map((f) => f.value),
  { yTitle: 'Long-term debt of the governments here', labelValues: true },
)
const rankSpec = bar(
  ranks.figures.map((f) => f.label),
  ranks.figures.map((f) => f.value),
  { yTitle: 'Dollars per resident', labelValues: true },
)
---

<Article slug="in-the-countys-name">
  <p>
    A county's own books say what the county spends. They do not say what it costs to be governed
    here, because a resident of Bath Township is governed by the county, the township, a school
    district, a career centre, a park district, a soil and water district and a transit authority,
    and each keeps its own accounts. One federal survey puts all of them on the same page in the
    same units. It also puts a number on this county that is larger than anything else about it.
  </p>

  <h2>Two billion two hundred million</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={two} open />
  <AssertionCard assertion={what} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={one} />
  <p>
    A hospital system borrows, and the borrowing is done in the county's name so that the lenders'
    interest is tax-exempt. The bonds are secured on the hospitals; the county's taxes secure
    nothing; on repayment the buildings belong to the borrower. Note 19 of every audit since 2010
    says so in the same sentence, and that sentence is the reason the number is not a liability of
    Allen County.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={first} open />
  <ChartFigure
    id="ohio"
    title="Industrial revenue debt per resident, 2017"
    caption="The three largest of the fifty-two Ohio counties carrying the item. Allen's figure is the county's own answer; Franklin's is the Bureau's estimate."
    columns={['County', 'Per resident']}
    rows={first.figures.map((f) => [f.label, `$${f.value.toLocaleString()}`])}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="ohio" set:html={JSON.stringify(ohioSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={check} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={gasb} open />
  <ChartFigure
    id="gasb"
    title="Conduit debt outstanding at 31 December"
    caption="The year between the two is the year the county adopted GASB Statement No. 91 and the note stopped naming borrowers."
    columns={['Date', 'Outstanding']}
    rows={gasb.figures.map((f) => [f.label, `$${f.value.toLocaleString()}`])}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="gasb" set:html={JSON.stringify(gasbSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={gone} />

  <h2>What it costs to be governed here</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={all} open />
  <AssertionCard assertion={halves} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={three} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={districts} />
  <p>
    The sixth largest government in the county buys health insurance for school employees and has
    no territory, no electorate and no building. The port authority raised thirty-six thousand
    dollars. Both are governments in the same sense the county is, because Ohio wrote them that way.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={ranks} open />
  <ChartFigure
    id="ranks"
    title="Local government revenue and spending per resident, 2022"
    caption="Allen County against the median of Ohio's eighty-eight, computed the same way for each."
    columns={['Measure', 'Per resident']}
    rows={ranks.figures.map((f) => [f.label, `$${f.value.toLocaleString()}`])}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="ranks" set:html={JSON.stringify(rankSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={deficit} />

  <h2>What they owe</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={owed} open />
  <AssertionCard assertion={nine} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={least} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={fall} open />
  <ChartFigure
    id="fall"
    title="Long-term debt of Allen County's governments"
    caption="The 2017 figure twice: as the Bureau published it, and on the definition the 2022 file uses."
    columns={['Basis', 'Amount']}
    rows={fall.figures.map((f) => [f.label, `$${f.value.toLocaleString()}`])}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="fall" set:html={JSON.stringify(fallSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={factor} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={liab} />

  <h2>The county did not answer</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={noanswer} open />
  <AssertionCard assertion={schools} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={rate} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={auditor} />
  <p>
    The county's treasurer never typed that figure. Nobody did. A model produced it because the
    county returned no questionnaire, and the only thing in the record that says so is the
    thirty-second character of a thirty-two character line — a letter that appears in no summary
    table and in no description of the column it qualifies.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={large} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={flag} />
  <p>
    Discarding the estimates is not the remedy, because the county would then hold five villages and
    four townships that raise nothing and spend nothing. What the estimates need is their flag,
    carried in the sentence rather than in a footnote, and a check against the governments next door
    that did answer.
  </p>
</Article>
